    <!-- The single GPU particle pass (r.GPUParticle.FixDeltaSeconds 0, the in-game menu's
         "Single GPU particle pass") without losing the fixed step of emitters whose local vector
         field asks for it (bUseFixDT, flag 8 at Simulation+0x1cc: PS_air_sparkles in Dan's crypt,
         leaves and fluff). Unpatched, 0 also turns their 1/30 s steps into one step of the frame
         time; patched, the game thread (FGPUSpriteParticleEmitterInstance's per-frame data,
         01.00 0x2382e50) always steps with the registered 1/30 s, and the single pass on the
         render thread (SimulateGPUParticles 0x2366cb0) runs as the fixed-step pass: the
         emitters' fixed-step parameters, read from and written to the same buffers as before,
         drawn from the buffer it writes (the cvar's 0 still drops the second, copying pass and
         reads the current state). Only the sub-step look-ahead of those few emitters is lost
         (they move in 1/30 s steps). With the cvar at its 1/30 default nothing changes, so the
         live switch (menu, toggle file second word 8192) still compares with the stock game.
         research/docs/study-particle-fixed-step.md. Off by default: run.py
         GOW3_PARTICLE_SINGLE_FIXED=1 / 0 switches it on / off (extra-env.txt). 01.02: the same
         bytes at +0x2dd0; the 1/30 constant at 0x3e276dc. -->
    <Metadata Title="MediEvil"
              Name="GPU particle fixed step in the single pass"
              Note="With the single GPU particle pass on, particle effects that the artists set to a fixed 1/30 s step (floating sparkles, leaves, fluff) keep it instead of stepping with the frame time. Needs the single pass to change anything."
